From f7a1b251de868d968fde70604bee81ef47de0fbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:07:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hub admission: judge courier landings, stay-here and
 structural hub keeps, relay-time owners

Review t_01a1ceabf1ca19c8 + spec owner decisions (11-12):
- routed (origin_intent) creates landing on the hub are judged before the create txn
  (courier_plan); a deny re-enrolls the card in the pool with requires hub:write
- placement=local/here, runs_on=[] and hub-only lease labels on the hub are explicit pins:
  a deny refuses; a structural keep-local on the hub is judged too (a deny refuses)
- runs_on string/padded/comma shapes naming machine:hub are normalized before the gate
- capability owners are judged at relay time, never inside the 30 s wait-check; an
  unavailable verdict fails retryably (the next route is a fresh relay generation)
- in-transaction denies (owner, move) are recorded as hub_admission events
- end-to-end provenance test through the real call_llm class router + native SDK
